# UI-PAN-1 (owner, 2026-11-16: "no click pan"): a press that moves less than the click slop
# (4 drawable pixels) moves the map not at all, with either button; a longer drag still pans. The
# owner's ui_4.mp4 showed a right click in demolish mode nudging the map by its jitter (4-7
# capture pixels). `camera.pans` counts pan() calls.
# Launch: --play data/maps/lan5.txt --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
wait frames 5
expect fact camera.pans == 0
# Clicks with a 3.6 px jitter, nothing armed: no pan.
ldrag_px 500 380 503 382
wait frames 3
expect fact camera.pans == 0
rdrag_px 500 380 503 382
wait frames 3
expect fact camera.pans == 0
# Real drags, both buttons: one pan each, the whole way from the press.
ldrag_px 500 380 540 400
wait frames 3
expect fact camera.pans == 1
rdrag_px 500 380 540 400
wait frames 3
expect fact camera.pans == 2
# The ui_4 case: demolish mode, a jittery right click - no pan, and the click turns the demolish
# mode off (UI-PLACE-2).
key b
wait frames 5
click_px 996 736
wait frames 3
expect fact tool.mode == demolish
rdrag_px 500 380 503 382
wait frames 3
expect fact camera.pans == 2
expect fact tool.mode == off
quit
